@startuml

title PENA POC 01 — Python Project Structure

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

skinparam package {
  BorderColor #2F5597
  BackgroundColor #F8FBFF
}

skinparam folder {
  BorderColor #2F5597
  BackgroundColor #F8FBFF
}

skinparam artifact {
  BorderColor #666666
  BackgroundColor #FFFCE8
}

package "pena-agent repository" {

  artifact "pyproject.toml" as PYPROJECT
  artifact "README.md" as README
  artifact ".env.example" as ENVEX
  artifact "config/poc01.yaml" as CONFIG

  package "src/pena" as SRC {
    artifact "__init__.py" as INIT
    artifact "cli.py" as CLI
    artifact "config.py" as CONFIGPY
    artifact "models.py" as MODELS

    package "ingestion" as INGESTION {
      artifact "reader.py" as READER
      artifact "normalizer.py" as NORMALIZER
    }

    package "summarization" as SUM {
      artifact "prompt_builder.py" as PROMPT
      artifact "llm_client.py" as LLMCLIENT
      artifact "summarizer.py" as SUMMARIZER
    }

    package "scoring" as SCORE {
      artifact "trust.py" as TRUST
      artifact "relevance.py" as REL
    }

    package "digest" as DIGEST {
      artifact "generator.py" as GENERATOR
      artifact "markdown_writer.py" as MDWRITER
    }

    package "observability" as OBS {
      artifact "run_report.py" as RUNREPORT
      artifact "logger.py" as LOGGER
    }

    package "learning" as LEARN {
      artifact "extractor.py" as EXTRACTOR
    }
  }

  package "tests" as TESTS {
    artifact "test_config.py" as TCONFIG
    artifact "test_ingestion.py" as TING
    artifact "test_digest.py" as TDIGEST
    artifact "test_scoring.py" as TSCORE
  }

}

CLI --> CONFIGPY : loads config
CONFIGPY --> CONFIG : reads
CLI --> READER : starts pipeline
READER --> NORMALIZER
NORMALIZER --> SUMMARIZER
SUMMARIZER --> PROMPT
SUMMARIZER --> LLMCLIENT
NORMALIZER --> TRUST
NORMALIZER --> REL
TRUST --> GENERATOR
REL --> GENERATOR
GENERATOR --> MDWRITER
GENERATOR --> RUNREPORT
RUNREPORT --> LOGGER
RUNREPORT --> EXTRACTOR

MODELS ..> INGESTION
MODELS ..> SUM
MODELS ..> SCORE
MODELS ..> DIGEST
MODELS ..> OBS
MODELS ..> LEARN

TESTS ..> SRC : validates deterministic boundaries

note bottom of SRC
POC 01 uses a simple Python module structure.
The goal is clarity, testability, and AI-readable boundaries.
end note

note right of PYPROJECT
pyproject.toml is the Python project metadata file.
It is the closest modern equivalent to package.json in this POC.
end note

@enduml
